# Bharat Dev Tools - Cursor Rules

## Project Overview

This is **Bharat Dev Tools** - a scalable, reusable, high-performance, mobile-first, pure JavaScript developer tools platform. The project uses NO frameworks - only vanilla JavaScript, HTML, and CSS.

**Goal**: Build a scalable, reusable, high-performance, mobile-first, pure JavaScript developer tools platform with shared components, analytics, observability, and strict quality standards.

---

## 1️⃣ Core Principles

Whenever Cursor generates or modifies code, it MUST:

- ✅ Follow **SOLID principles**
- ✅ Ensure **high reusability**
- ✅ Maintain **scalable architecture**
- ✅ Follow **modular structure**
- ✅ Write **clean, readable, maintainable JavaScript**
- ✅ Avoid **vendor lock-in**; prefer free & open tech
- ✅ Favor **performance, UX consistency, and security**
- ✅ This entire project is **pure JavaScript** — no frameworks unless explicitly requested
- ✅ **Less coupled code** - Minimize dependencies between modules
- ✅ **Function names must clearly describe their purpose**
- ✅ **Reduce complexity** - Minimize if/else nesting (use early returns, guard clauses)
- ✅ **Comprehensive error tracking** - Log all failures with analytics
- ✅ **Production-ready code** - All code must be production-ready (no debug code, no console.log, no exposed secrets)

---

## 1️⃣.1 Production Code Standards

**CRITICAL RULES - All code must be production-ready:**

### 1.1.1 No Console Logging

**Rules**:
- ✅ **NEVER use `console.log()` in production code**
- ✅ **NEVER use `console.debug()`, `console.info()`, `console.warn()` in production**
- ✅ **Use analytics tracking instead** for important events
- ✅ **Use Sentry for error logging** instead of console.error
- ✅ **Debug code must be wrapped in debug scope** (see below)

**Example - Bad**:
```javascript
// ❌ BAD: Console.log in production code
function formatJSON(text) {
  console.log('Formatting JSON:', text); // ❌ REMOVE
  return JSON.stringify(JSON.parse(text), null, 2);
}
```

**Example - Good**:
```javascript
// ✅ GOOD: Use analytics or remove
function formatJSON(text) {
  // Track via analytics if needed
  if (typeof window.Analytics !== 'undefined') {
    window.Analytics.trackFormatJson({ input_length: text.length });
  }
  return JSON.stringify(JSON.parse(text), null, 2);
}
```

### 1.1.2 Debug Code Scope

**Rules**:
- ✅ **All debug code MUST be wrapped in debug scope**
- ✅ **Use environment detection** to enable/disable debug code
- ✅ **Debug code should be removed or disabled in production**

**Debug Scope Pattern**:
```javascript
// ✅ GOOD: Debug code in debug scope
const DEBUG_MODE = window.location.hostname === 'localhost' || 
                   window.location.hostname === '127.0.0.1' ||
                   window.location.search.includes('debug=true');

function formatJSON(text) {
  if (DEBUG_MODE) {
    console.log('[DEBUG] Formatting JSON:', text.substring(0, 100));
  }
  
  // Production code here
  return JSON.stringify(JSON.parse(text), null, 2);
}

// Or use a debug utility
const Debug = {
  log: (...args) => {
    if (DEBUG_MODE) {
      console.log('[DEBUG]', ...args);
    }
  },
  error: (...args) => {
    if (DEBUG_MODE) {
      console.error('[DEBUG]', ...args);
    }
  }
};

// Usage
Debug.log('Processing input:', input);
```

### 1.1.3 No Exposed Sensitive Information

**Rules**:
- ✅ **NEVER expose API keys, secrets, or sensitive data**
- ✅ **NEVER hardcode credentials** in source code
- ✅ **NEVER expose internal URLs or endpoints** that shouldn't be public
- ✅ **NEVER log sensitive user data** (passwords, tokens, PII)
- ✅ **Use environment variables or config files** for sensitive data (if needed)

**Example - Bad**:
```javascript
// ❌ BAD: Exposed API key
const API_KEY = 'sk_live_1234567890abcdef'; // ❌ NEVER DO THIS

// ❌ BAD: Exposed internal endpoint
const INTERNAL_API = 'https://internal.company.com/api'; // ❌ NEVER DO THIS
```

**Example - Good**:
```javascript
// ✅ GOOD: Use config with safe defaults
const API_CONFIG = window.APP_CONFIG?.API_CONFIG || {
  // Safe defaults or empty
};

// ✅ GOOD: No sensitive data in code
// All sensitive data should be server-side or in secure config
```

### 1.1.4 Bundle Splitting & Code Splitting

**Rules**:
- ✅ **Implement bundle splitting** for faster page load
- ✅ **Lazy load non-critical JavaScript** modules
- ✅ **Split large utilities** into separate files
- ✅ **Load heavy libraries on demand** (CodeMirror, large dependencies)
- ✅ **Use dynamic imports** for code splitting

**Bundle Splitting Pattern**:
```javascript
// ✅ GOOD: Lazy load heavy dependencies
async function loadCodeMirror() {
  if (window.CodeMirror) {
    return Promise.resolve();
  }
  
  // Load CodeMirror only when needed
  await Promise.all([
    loadScript('https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/codemirror/5.65.5/codemirror.min.js'),
    loadScript('https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/codemirror/5.65.5/mode/javascript/javascript.min.js')
  ]);
}

// Load on demand
document.getElementById('input-editor').addEventListener('focus', async () => {
  await loadCodeMirror();
  initializeEditor();
});

// ✅ GOOD: Dynamic imports for code splitting
async function loadFormatter() {
  const { formatJSON, minifyJSON } = await import('./assets/js/formatter.js');
  return { formatJSON, minifyJSON };
}

// Use when needed
const formatter = await loadFormatter();
formatter.formatJSON(text);
```

**Script Loading Strategy**:
```html
<!-- Critical: Load immediately -->
<script src="assets/js/theme.js"></script>
<script type="module" src="assets/js/config.js"></script>

<!-- Non-critical: Defer loading -->
<script src="assets/js/analytics.js" defer></script>
<script src="assets/js/version.js" defer></script>

<!-- Heavy libraries: Load on demand or defer -->
<script src="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/codemirror/5.65.5/codemirror.min.js" defer></script>
```

### 1.1.5 Production-Ready Code Checklist

**Before committing, ensure**:
- ✅ **No console.log statements** (use analytics or debug scope)
- ✅ **No exposed secrets or sensitive data**
- ✅ **No debug code** (or wrapped in debug scope)
- ✅ **No commented-out code** (remove or document why it's there)
- ✅ **No TODO comments** (complete the task or create an issue)
- ✅ **No test data or mock data** in production code
- ✅ **Error handling is complete** (no unhandled errors)
- ✅ **All code is tested** (unit tests pass)
- ✅ **Performance is optimized** (bundle splitting, lazy loading)
- ✅ **Security checks pass** (no XSS vulnerabilities, input validation)

