## 6️⃣ Analytics & Observability

### Google Analytics 4 (GA4)

**Configuration**: `/assets/js/analytics.js`

**Rules**:
- ✅ Every new page MUST include Analytics script
- ✅ NO inline GA config
- ✅ NO duplicated GA instances
- ✅ Analytics automatically disabled on localhost
- ✅ **Page load time automatically tracked** ✅

**Error Event Tracking**:
Add these events to `ANALYTICS_EVENTS` in `analytics.js`:
```javascript
VALIDATION_ERROR: 'validation_error',
FORMAT_ERROR: 'format_error',
UI_FREEZE: 'ui_freeze',
OPERATION_FAILED: 'operation_failed'
```

### Sentry Error Tracking

**Rules**:
- ✅ MUST track crashes, traces & important events
- ✅ Config in `/assets/js/version.js`
- ✅ Use `logErrorToSentry()` helper pattern
- ✅ Include context (tags, extra data)

---

## 7️⃣ Coding Standards

### JavaScript

- ✅ **ES6+ only**
- ✅ **`const` / `let` ONLY** - No `var`
- ✅ **Modular code** - Use ES6 modules
- ✅ **2-space indentation**
- ✅ **Semicolons required**

### Function Naming

- ✅ **Verb-noun pattern**: `formatJSON`, `validateInput`
- ✅ **Boolean functions**: `isValid`, `hasError`
- ✅ **Event handlers**: `formatHandler`, `minifyHandler`
- ✅ **Clear, descriptive names** - No abbreviations

### Complexity Reduction

- ✅ **Early returns** - Reduce nesting
- ✅ **Guard clauses** - Validate early
- ✅ **Extract complex conditions** - Named functions
- ✅ **Max 2-3 levels of nesting**

---

## 8️⃣ Page Creation Checklist

When creating a new page:

### 8.1 Core Requirements

1. ✅ Include Header + Footer components  
   - **Footer = All tools + footer**: Loading `footer.css` and `footer.js` adds both the **All tools** section (buttons linking to each tool) and the site footer. Every new page MUST include these so the All tools section appears above the footer:
   ```html
   <link rel="stylesheet" href="components/footer.css">
   <script src="components/footer.js"></script>
   ```
   - From a page in a subdirectory (e.g. `jsondiff/index.html`), use `../components/footer.css` and `../components/footer.js`. The footer script resolves asset paths automatically.
2. ✅ Include Analytics script (defer)
3. ✅ Include Sentry script (defer)
4. ✅ Include Theme script
5. ✅ Add page to `PAGE_NAMES` in `analytics.js`
6. ✅ Implement UI freeze detection for heavy operations
7. ✅ Add error tracking with analytics
8. ✅ Create test file in `/test/`
9. ✅ Register tests in `run-all-tests.js`
10. ✅ Ensure mobile responsive
11. ✅ **Register tool on "Our Developer Tools" page** (`tools.html`) - See Section 8.4
12. ✅ **Update `sitemap.xml`** to include the new page URL with appropriate `priority`, `changefreq`, and `lastmod`

### 8.2 SEO Requirements

**CRITICAL - Every page MUST include:**

1. ✅ **Title with "Free" keyword**:
   ```html
   <title>Free [Tool Name] Online | [Description] | No Sign Up Required</title>
   ```
   Example: `Free JSON Formatter Online | Beautify, Minify & Validate JSON | No Sign Up`

2. ✅ **Meta Description with "Free" keyword**:
   ```html
   <meta name="description" content="Free [tool description]. [Key features]. No sign up required. [Benefits].">
   ```

3. ✅ **FAQ Section with SEO Keywords**:
   - ✅ Include **important and common keywords** in FAQ questions
   - ✅ FAQ should answer **common user queries**
   - ✅ Use **natural language** with target keywords
   - ✅ Include **structured data (FAQPage schema)** for rich snippets
   
   **FAQ Pattern**:
   ```html
   <!-- FAQ Section -->
   <section class="faq-section" id="faq">
     <div class="faq-container">
       <h2 class="section-title">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
       <div class="faq-list">
         <div class="faq-item">
           <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
             <span>What is [tool name] and how does it work?</span>
             <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
           </button>
           <div class="faq-answer">
             <p>[Answer with keywords naturally integrated]</p>
           </div>
         </div>
         <!-- More FAQ items -->
       </div>
     </div>
   </section>
   
   <!-- FAQPage Schema for SEO -->
   <script type="application/ld+json">
   {
     "@context": "https://schema.org",
     "@type": "FAQPage",
     "mainEntity": [
       {
         "@type": "Question",
         "name": "What is [tool name]?",
         "acceptedAnswer": {
           "@type": "Answer",
           "text": "[Answer with keywords]"
         }
       }
     ]
   }
   </script>
   ```

4. ✅ **Structured Data (JSON-LD)**:
   - ✅ WebApplication schema
   - ✅ BreadcrumbList schema
   - ✅ FAQPage schema (if FAQ exists)
   - ✅ HowTo schema (if applicable)

5. ✅ **Open Graph & Twitter Cards**:
   ```html
   <meta property="og:title" content="Free [Tool Name] Online | [Description]">
   <meta property="og:description" content="[Description with Free keyword]">
   <meta property="og:type" content="website">
   <meta property="og:url" content="https://bharatdevtool.com/[page].html">
   <meta property="og:image" content="https://bharatdevtool.com/assets/img/og/og-image.jpg">
   <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image">
   ```

6. ✅ **Canonical URL**:
   ```html
   <link rel="canonical" href="https://bharatdevtool.com/[page].html">
   ```

7. ✅ **Sitemap Registration**:
   - ✅ Add page to `sitemap.xml`
   - ✅ Ensure proper priority and changefreq

8. ✅ **Robots Meta** (if needed):
   ```html
   <meta name="robots" content="index, follow">
   <meta name="googlebot" content="index, follow">
   ```

### 8.3 SEO Keyword Strategy

**Title/Subtitle Pattern**:
- ✅ **Always include "Free"** in title
- ✅ Include **primary keyword** (tool name)
- ✅ Include **action keywords** (Online, Tool, Generator, Converter, etc.)
- ✅ Include **benefit keywords** (No Sign Up, Instant, Secure, etc.)

**Examples**:
- ✅ `Free JSON Formatter Online | Beautify, Minify & Validate JSON | No Sign Up`
- ✅ `Free Base64 Encoder/Decoder | Encode & Decode Base64 Online | Instant Results`
- ✅ `Free QR Code Generator | Create QR Codes Online | No Registration Required`

**FAQ Keywords**:
- Include questions with: "How to", "What is", "Can I", "Does it"
- Include answers with: tool name, "free", "online", "no sign up", key features
- Use natural language, not keyword stuffing

### 8.4 Register Tool on "Our Developer Tools" Page

**CRITICAL - Every new tool MUST be added to `/tools.html`:**

When creating a new tool/page from scratch, you MUST:

1. ✅ **Add Feature Card** to `tools.html`:
   - Add a new `<div class="feature-card">` in the features grid
   - Include: icon, title, description, example, action buttons
   - Follow the existing pattern from other tools

2. ✅ **Update ItemList Schema** in `tools.html`:
   - Add new entry to the `ItemList` structured data (JSON-LD)
   - Include: position, name, URL
   - Update position numbers for all subsequent items

3. ✅ **Feature Card Template**:
   ```html
   <div class="feature-card">
     <div class="feature-icon">[ICON]</div>
     <h3 class="feature-title">[Tool Name]</h3>
     <p class="feature-description">[Brief description of what the tool does and its key features]</p>
     <div class="feature-example">
       <strong>Example:</strong>
       <code>[Input example]</code> → <code>[Output example]</code>
     </div>
     <div class="feature-actions">
       <a href="[tool-page].html" class="feature-btn">Try [Tool Name] →</a>
       <a href="[documentation-url]" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="feature-link">[Documentation Link Text] →</a>
     </div>
   </div>
   ```

4. ✅ **ItemList Schema Entry**:
   ```json
   {
     "@type": "ListItem",
     "position": [NEXT_NUMBER],
     "name": "[Tool Name]",
     "url": "https://bharatdevtool.com/[tool-page].html"
   }
   ```

5. ✅ **Icon Selection**:
   - Choose appropriate emoji icon that represents the tool
   - Examples: 📄 (JSON), 🔗 (URL/Deeplink), 📱 (QR Code), 🔍 (Decoder), etc.

6. ✅ **Description Guidelines**:
   - Keep description concise (2-3 sentences)
   - Highlight key features and benefits
   - Mention "free" and "online" naturally
   - Include what makes it useful for developers

**Example - Adding a new Base64 tool**:
```html
<!-- Feature Card -->
<div class="feature-card">
  <div class="feature-icon">🔐</div>
  <h3 class="feature-title">Base64 Encoder/Decoder</h3>
  <p class="feature-description">Encode and decode Base64 strings instantly. Perfect for encoding binary data, API tokens, and data transmission. Supports text, images, and files.</p>
  <div class="feature-example">
    <strong>Example:</strong>
    <code>Hello World</code> → <code>SGVsbG8gV29ybGQ=</code>
  </div>
  <div class="feature-actions">
    <a href="base64.html" class="feature-btn">Try Base64 Encoder →</a>
    <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/btoa" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="feature-link">Base64 Docs (MDN) →</a>
  </div>
</div>
```

```json
// ItemList Schema Entry
{
  "@type": "ListItem",
  "position": 8,
  "name": "Base64 Encoder/Decoder",
  "url": "https://bharatdevtool.com/base64.html"
}
```

**Checklist**:
- ✅ Feature card added to `tools.html`
- ✅ ItemList schema updated in `tools.html`
- ✅ Icon selected and added
- ✅ Description written with SEO keywords
- ✅ Example provided
- ✅ Action buttons link to correct pages
- ✅ Documentation link added (if applicable)

---

## 9️⃣ Quality Checklist

Before committing code:

### 9.1 Code Quality

- ✅ **Loose coupling** - Minimal dependencies
- ✅ **Clear function names** - Self-documenting
- ✅ **Reduced complexity** - Early returns, guard clauses
- ✅ **Error tracking** - All failures logged with analytics
- ✅ **UI freeze detection** - Heavy operations monitored
- ✅ **Performance** - Debounced/throttled where needed
- ✅ **Memory management** - Cleanup on destroy
- ✅ **Accessibility** - ARIA labels, keyboard navigation
- ✅ **Security** - Input validation, XSS prevention
- ✅ **Tests** - Unit + integration tests
- ✅ **Documentation** - JSDoc comments

### 9.2 Production Readiness

- ✅ **No console.log** - Use analytics or debug scope
- ✅ **No exposed secrets** - No API keys, credentials, sensitive data
- ✅ **No debug code** - Or wrapped in debug scope
- ✅ **Bundle splitting** - Code split for faster loads
- ✅ **Production-ready** - All code is production-ready

### 9.3 SEO & Page Requirements

- ✅ **Title with "Free" keyword** - Attractive, keyword-rich title
- ✅ **FAQ section** - With important SEO keywords
- ✅ **Structured data** - JSON-LD schemas (WebApplication, FAQPage, etc.)
- ✅ **Open Graph tags** - Social media preview
- ✅ **Canonical URL** - Proper canonical tag
- ✅ **Sitemap updated** - Page added to sitemap.xml
- ✅ **Meta description** - With "Free" keyword and benefits
- ✅ **Tool registered** - Added to "Our Developer Tools" page (`tools.html`)

### 9.4 UI/UX

- ✅ **Good UI design** - Modern, clean, intuitive
- ✅ **Minor animations** - Subtle, performant animations
- ✅ **Performance maintained** - No performance degradation
- ✅ **Mobile responsive** - Works on all devices
- ✅ **Accessibility** - Keyboard navigation, screen readers

---

## 🎯 Summary

**Core Quality Principles**:
1. **Less Coupled Code** - Minimize dependencies
2. **Clear Function Names** - Self-documenting code
3. **Reduce Complexity** - Early returns, guard clauses
4. **Comprehensive Error Tracking** - Analytics on all failures
5. **Page Load Time** - ✅ Already implemented automatically
6. **UI Freeze Detection** - Monitor and log UI freezes

**Additional Quality**:
- Performance optimization (debounce, throttle, Web Workers)
- Memory management (cleanup, no leaks)
- Accessibility (a11y standards)
- Security (input validation, XSS prevention)
- Testing (unit, integration, edge cases)
- Documentation (JSDoc, inline comments)
- Production-ready code (no console.log, no secrets, debug scope)
- Bundle splitting for faster page loads
- SEO optimization (FAQ, structured data, "Free" keyword)
- UI/UX with performant animations

**Production Code Standards**:
1. **No console.log** - Use analytics or debug scope
2. **No exposed secrets** - Never expose API keys or sensitive data
3. **Bundle splitting** - Split code for faster loads
4. **Debug scope** - All debug code in debug scope
5. **Production-ready** - All code must be production-ready

**Page Creation Requirements**:
1. **FAQ with SEO keywords** - Include important keywords naturally
2. **SEO optimization** - Title with "Free", structured data, sitemap
3. **Good UI with animations** - Modern design with subtle, performant animations
4. **Register on Tools page** - Add feature card and ItemList entry to `tools.html`

**Remember**: This is a pure JavaScript project. Keep it simple, modular, performant, maintainable, and production-ready.

